Notes
-----

The server components depend on several of the permissively licensed crates.
Combining MIT or Apache-2.0 code into an AGPL-3.0 work is permitted; the
resulting combined work is AGPL-3.0-or-later, while those crates remain
available on their own terms.

The dependency never runs the other way. No client or protocol crate links an
AGPL-licensed crate in a shipped build, and none may be made to; this is
enforced by a test, crates/trace-commons-server/tests/license_boundary.rs.
`trace-commons-contributor` does take a test-only dev-dependency on
`trace-commons-server` on non-Windows targets. Dev-dependencies are not part of
any published artifact, so that edge conveys no combined work and imposes no
AGPL obligation on the contributor crate.

Contributions made before this split remain available under the MIT and
Apache-2.0 terms that applied when they were published.


Inbound contributions
---------------------

Contributions to this repository are licensed to the project under
`MIT OR Apache-2.0` -- including contributions to the AGPL-licensed server
crates. Contributors retain their copyright; nothing is assigned.

This is intentionally not "inbound = outbound". Recipients of the server crates
still receive them under the AGPL and owe its obligations. Licensing
contributions in permissively means the project keeps the ability to relicense
what it distributes, which a single outside contribution under AGPL-only terms
would otherwise remove permanently.

See CONTRIBUTING.md.
